{
 "id": "s4-l6",
 "stage": 4,
 "lesson": 6,
 "title": {
  "de": "Das Objekt: 을/를",
  "en": "The object: 을/를"
 },
 "intro": {
  "de": "을/를 markiert das Objekt, also das, was gegessen, gekauft oder gesehen wird. Nach Konsonant steht 을, nach Vokal 를: 책을, 커피를.\nDie Reihenfolge ist: wer – was – Verb. 저는 커피를 마셔요 = Ich trinke Kaffee.\nIm Gespräch fällt 을/를 oft weg. Zum Lernen schreibst du es aber mit.",
  "en": "을/를 marks the object: the thing being eaten, bought or seen. Use 을 after a consonant and 를 after a vowel: 책을, 커피를.\nThe order is: who – what – verb. 저는 커피를 마셔요 = I drink coffee.\nIn conversation 을/를 is often dropped, but while learning, keep it in."
 },
 "exercises": [
  "see-meaning",
  "pick-hangul",
  "build-sentence"
 ],
 "check": {
  "questions": 8
 },
